# Node
node_modules/

# NOTE: dist/ is the `vite build` output and is NOT tracked. It must EXIST at
# compile time: src-tauri/Cargo.toml sets `default = ["custom-protocol", ...]`,
# which forces Tauri's generate_context! into production mode on every build
# (including `tauri dev`), and that reads frontendDist ("../dist") from
# tauri.conf.json. So it has to be built, but it does not have to be committed:
# both CI lanes run `npm ci && npm run build` before the Rust build
# (build-msvc.yml, build-linux.yml), which regenerates it. `beforeBuildCommand`
# is only `echo skip`, so that CI step is the sole thing producing dist/.
# A LOCAL build must run `npm run build` first or cargo check will fail on the
# missing frontendDist.

# Vite config temp files
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs
vite.config.*.timestamp-*

# Rustup toolchain config (machine-local)
/.rustup/
